WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.338 --> 00:00:20.261
It was August 19—National Potato Day!

2
00:00:20.262 --> 00:00:32.731
The family was going to the Potato Festival.

3
00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:38.395
"First, I'll drop off my potato soup for the cooking contest," said Dad.

4
00:00:38.396 --> 00:00:44.456
He took a big pot out of the car.

5
00:00:44.457 --> 00:00:54.372
"Let's walk around while Dad goes to the judges' tent," said Mom.

6
00:00:54.373 --> 00:00:58.665
At the first booth was a big world map.

7
00:00:58.666 --> 00:01:05.363
"It says potatoes came from the Andes Mountains in South America," said Kate.

8
00:01:05.364 --> 00:01:11.986
"Early explorers took them to Europe and Asia."

9
00:01:11.987 --> 00:01:17.869
"Potatoes kept thousands of Europeans from starving," said Mom.

10
00:01:17.870 --> 00:01:21.517
"But look," said Seth, pointing at the map.

11
00:01:21.518 --> 00:01:27.941
"Europeans took potatoes to North America."

12
00:01:27.942 --> 00:01:32.301
"Potatoes grow well in many places," said Mom.

13
00:01:32.302 --> 00:01:36.245
"They're one of the world's largest food crops."

14
00:01:36.246 --> 00:01:40.680
"Enough geography," said Seth.

15
00:01:40.681 --> 00:01:42.849
"Let's eat!"

16
00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:46.837
"We're waiting for Dad," said Kate.

17
00:01:46.838 --> 00:01:49.936
They walked to another booth.

18
00:01:49.937 --> 00:01:58.076
A sign read: "What Can You Do with a Potato?"

19
00:01:58.077 --> 00:02:05.998
"Wow! You can polish shoes and remove rust with potatoes," said Mom.

20
00:02:05.999 --> 00:02:08.643
"This is cool," said Kate.

21
00:02:08.644 --> 00:02:15.693
"You can make glue."

22
00:02:15.694 --> 00:02:18.080
"Look at this!" called Seth.

23
00:02:18.081 --> 00:02:22.248
They watched a man stick two pieces of metal into a potato.

24
00:02:22.249 --> 00:02:24.886
He connected wires to the metal pieces.

25
00:02:24.887 --> 00:02:27.580
A small lightbulb lit up!

26
00:02:27.581 --> 00:02:31.438
"It's a potato battery," said Seth.

27
00:02:31.439 --> 00:02:37.275
"A potato can power a small lightbulb for about forty days," said the man.

28
00:02:37.276 --> 00:02:39.919
"Cool!" said Seth.

29
00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:43.563
"A potato costs a lot less than batteries!"

30
00:02:43.564 --> 00:02:46.757
Seth's stomach growled.

31
00:02:46.758 --> 00:02:51.290
"Sounds like you need to power up," said Mom.

32
00:02:51.291 --> 00:02:55.218
"There's Dad at the French fry booth."

33
00:02:55.219 --> 00:02:59.938
They hurried over.

34
00:02:59.939 --> 00:03:05.499
Dad grinned. "I'm discovering how to eat French fries."

35
00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:07.877
"It's easy," said Seth.

36
00:03:07.878 --> 00:03:11.738
"You dip them in ketchup."

37
00:03:11.739 --> 00:03:16.190
"In the Philippines they use banana ketchup," said Dad.

38
00:03:16.191 --> 00:03:19.311
"The English put vinegar on them.

39
00:03:19.312 --> 00:03:22.970
And in France they use mustard."

40
00:03:22.971 --> 00:03:27.524
"Were French fries invented in France?" asked Kate.

41
00:03:27.525 --> 00:03:35.324
"Nobody is sure," said Dad.

42
00:03:35.325 --> 00:03:38.256
"Thomas Jefferson first ate them in France.

43
00:03:38.257 --> 00:03:45.751
He loved them.

44
00:03:45.752 --> 00:03:53.808
He even served French fries at the White House."

45
00:03:53.809 --> 00:03:57.823
Kate ordered curly fries and Seth got waffle fries.

46
00:03:57.824 --> 00:04:05.706
Mom and Dad got steak fries.

47
00:04:05.707 --> 00:04:12.312
Seth licked ketchup from his fingers. "I'm full—until dinner."

48
00:04:12.313 --> 00:04:15.131
Dad grinned and held up a blue ribbon.

49
00:04:15.132 --> 00:04:22.443
"Tonight we're having Dad's prize-winning potato soup!"
